WEBVTT

00:05.080 --> 00:06.480
It's the ocean!

00:06.480 --> 00:07.730
Vacation!

00:07.730 --> 00:09.530
Island!

00:12.690 --> 00:13.950
This is refreshing.

00:13.950 --> 00:18.320
Isn't it nice to forget the hustle and bustle of the city and to relax once in a while?

00:20.040 --> 00:21.750
Ouka!

00:21.750 --> 00:22.410
What was that?

00:22.410 --> 00:23.830
Look, look, look, look!

00:25.490 --> 00:26.210
That's...

00:27.330 --> 00:28.960
A pirate ship!

01:50.310 --> 01:51.750
Do you know the family frenzy?

01:51.750 --> 01:53.750
They're famous for running around the neighborhood.

01:53.750 --> 01:54.880
The world is a mess.

01:54.880 --> 01:56.630
Pay attention, else you'll get stabbed in the back.

02:14.840 --> 02:17.370
Innocent Pirate Mujyakey!

02:19.370 --> 02:20.680
Looks like they've arrived.

02:20.680 --> 02:22.260
"A-Arrived"?

02:22.260 --> 02:23.830
They're pirates!

02:23.830 --> 02:25.240
They're pirates, I tell you!

02:25.240 --> 02:27.660
All right! Mark your targets on the pirate ship!

02:27.660 --> 02:29.020
Ready to fire!

02:29.020 --> 02:30.100
Ready to fire.

02:30.100 --> 02:31.880
No, no! Stop provoking them!

02:31.880 --> 02:33.410
What's cheap today?

02:33.410 --> 02:34.800
Hey, you're not at a fish market!

02:34.800 --> 02:37.130
Welcome. We've got lots of mackerel today.

02:37.130 --> 02:39.090
Why are you all playing along with him?!

02:39.880 --> 02:41.390
Step back, amateur.

02:41.390 --> 02:42.640
We're professionals on the sea.

02:42.640 --> 02:45.630
We sell better fish than any fishermen out there.

02:45.630 --> 02:46.360
Oh...

02:46.360 --> 02:50.020
And we strive to be pirates that don't resort to violence and are loved by everyone.

02:50.020 --> 02:52.530
Wouldn't that defy the definition of pirates?

02:52.530 --> 02:56.730
I was moved by their idealism, so I started trading with them.

02:57.270 --> 02:57.970
I see...

02:59.070 --> 03:00.370
What's going on?

03:00.370 --> 03:01.860
Mother, that would be mackerel.

03:01.860 --> 03:02.840
Mackerel, huh?

03:02.840 --> 03:05.620
Oh no! All of this won't fit in the refrigerator!

03:05.620 --> 03:06.620
In that case!

03:07.400 --> 03:09.920
Shinmusouen style, Rain of Mackerel!

03:16.210 --> 03:18.810
I'll have one, too.

03:20.650 --> 03:22.220
Gekka...

03:22.220 --> 03:23.770
Gekka!!!

03:23.770 --> 03:25.170
I won't forgive you!

03:25.170 --> 03:27.220
Kyouka, be more mature.

03:30.680 --> 03:33.190
I'm simply hungry, Mom.

03:33.190 --> 03:34.720
Gekka's being mean.

03:34.720 --> 03:37.770
Just watching how you eat them makes me happy!

03:42.470 --> 03:44.640
Gekka! You dare revolt against your parents?

03:44.640 --> 03:48.990
Don't come to me if you get food poisoning from eating so much mackerel!

03:48.990 --> 03:50.580
You daughter of a bitch!

03:50.150 --> 03:52.000
What's the argument here about?

03:52.000 --> 03:53.000
Who?

03:53.000 --> 04:00.280
I've swept across the seven seas, stolen countless treasures, and am the feared captain of the Purple Skull Pirates,

04:00.280 --> 04:02.220
Mujyakey Serpent!

04:02.220 --> 04:02.720
Where are you?

04:02.720 --> 04:03.280
Over here!

04:03.280 --> 04:03.750
Where?

04:03.750 --> 04:04.220
Here!

04:04.220 --> 04:04.900
Where?

04:04.900 --> 04:05.430
Here!!

04:05.430 --> 04:06.710
Where?!

04:06.710 --> 04:07.510
Here!!!

04:07.510 --> 04:08.670
Where?!?!

04:08.670 --> 04:10.380
I said here!!!

04:14.310 --> 04:16.070
Inside the mackerel?

04:16.520 --> 04:19.000
What do you think you're doing, offloading me with the cargo?!

04:19.000 --> 04:20.060
Stupid! Idiots!

04:20.060 --> 04:20.900
Sorry, Captain.

04:20.900 --> 04:21.830
Captain?

04:21.830 --> 04:22.710
Yes.

04:22.710 --> 04:26.240
Mujyakey-san is the captain of the Purple Skull Pirates.

04:26.240 --> 04:26.950
Ehem!

04:26.950 --> 04:28.780
She's definitely shorter than Yuuka.

04:28.780 --> 04:30.380
Welcome back, Mom.

04:30.380 --> 04:34.270
Mujyakey-sama's the daughter of our former captain, Growald.

04:34.270 --> 04:35.560
Though she stinks like fish now.

04:35.560 --> 04:37.390
Don't say that!

04:37.390 --> 04:39.460
We'll follow you anywhere, Captain.

04:39.460 --> 04:40.620
Even if you stink like fish a little.

04:40.620 --> 04:42.470
Stop saying I stink like fish!

04:42.470 --> 04:44.630
Even the fish smell is charming, Captain.

04:44.630 --> 04:46.390
Y-You think so?

04:47.970 --> 04:49.930
Mujyakey-sama!

04:49.990 --> 04:51.850
Mujyakey-sama!

04:51.850 --> 04:54.970
Fish-stink Mujyakey-sama!

04:58.080 --> 04:58.810
That's...

04:58.810 --> 05:00.230
That's Do Gone!

05:06.990 --> 05:09.530
I've swept across the seven seas,

05:09.530 --> 05:10.990
killed countless enemies,

05:10.990 --> 05:13.410
and am the captain of the Burning Pirates,

05:13.410 --> 05:15.660
Red Blood Do Gone!

05:16.120 --> 05:18.120
Look, another weirdo.

05:18.120 --> 05:19.250
What are they supposed to be?

05:19.250 --> 05:24.130
Do Gone was an officer for Growald, noted to be his right-hand man.

05:24.130 --> 05:27.510
But the moment he passed away and Mujyakey-sama succeeded the seat,

05:27.590 --> 05:28.800
he betrayed us!

05:29.680 --> 05:33.550
We were supposed to be bound by
a bond tighter than that of a family!

05:33.550 --> 05:34.980
He's now a...

05:34.980 --> 05:37.400
Hey, what's a traitor doing here?!

05:37.400 --> 05:39.890
You know what I'm here for!

05:39.890 --> 05:43.480
Hand over the treasure map Growald left with you!

05:43.480 --> 05:45.060
Treasure?!

05:44.170 --> 05:47.150
Hey now Kyouka. Don't react to others' treasure.

05:47.150 --> 05:50.120
Why do you know about the treasure map?

05:50.860 --> 05:53.990
Right when he was about to die and was groggy,

05:53.990 --> 05:58.210
I asked him, "Captain, would you happen to have any treasure maps?"

05:58.210 --> 06:00.250
Then he kindly answered me.

06:00.250 --> 06:01.880
Th-That's impossible!

06:01.880 --> 06:02.700
Why you!

06:02.700 --> 06:03.380
So dirty of you!

06:03.380 --> 06:04.210
You dirty thief!

06:04.210 --> 06:05.830
You're cheap!

06:05.830 --> 06:08.470
Why are they yelling at each other?

06:09.290 --> 06:11.860
That's right, I have the treasure map right here!

06:11.860 --> 06:12.430
Captain!

06:12.430 --> 06:14.870
This makes things easy.

06:14.870 --> 06:16.360
Hand it over right now!

06:16.360 --> 06:18.940
To a person who is so ungrateful and a traitor and a big-eater and...

06:19.310 --> 06:23.110
...writes love poems secretly as a hobby as well as **** and **** and... and...

06:23.110 --> 06:24.210
Wait, now that's...

06:24.210 --> 06:27.940
and you even got your wife **** you, and you're such a **** human!

06:27.940 --> 06:31.330
I can't give this treasure to a person like you!

06:31.990 --> 06:33.740
Chut up! Chut up! Chut up!

06:33.740 --> 06:35.620
There's no point in what you say!

06:35.620 --> 06:36.570
I'm a pirate!

06:36.570 --> 06:39.710
Pirates get whatever they want using whatever means possible!

06:39.710 --> 06:45.230
No matter who cries or what other people say, we're thieves that know what we do is bad!

06:44.280 --> 06:45.230
You're wrong!

06:45.230 --> 06:47.090
Pirates are not supposed to do such things!

06:47.090 --> 06:48.940
This treasure is-

06:48.940 --> 06:49.510
Eh?

06:49.510 --> 06:50.850
It's mine!

06:50.850 --> 06:52.260
Hey! Kyouka, give it back to her!

06:52.260 --> 06:54.260
This now belongs to me.

06:54.260 --> 06:56.770
Everyone, let's go treasure hunting!

06:55.240 --> 06:56.400
Gomu Gomu no...

06:56.400 --> 06:56.770
Arm

06:58.060 --> 06:59.270
So stretchy!

06:59.360 --> 07:01.230
The treasure map is in my hands!

07:01.230 --> 07:02.570
Let go of Kyouka!

07:02.570 --> 07:04.170
Give back the map!

07:04.810 --> 07:11.280
Don't worry. Unlike immature you,
I will make a good use of Growald's assets.

07:11.280 --> 07:11.860
Fire!

07:16.040 --> 07:18.240
Can I fire? I can, right, Father?

07:18.240 --> 07:20.330
Not right now. If you hit Kyouka by mistake...

07:20.330 --> 07:21.080
You can't!

07:24.810 --> 07:27.380
In this world, the winner's whoever seizes it.

07:32.030 --> 07:33.420
Sorry, Father.

07:33.420 --> 07:35.090
Anyway, we must chase them.

07:35.090 --> 07:36.340
But how?

07:36.340 --> 07:37.310
Well...

07:42.240 --> 07:44.140
My men. We need to go after them right away.

07:44.140 --> 07:45.060
Aye aye, Sir!

07:46.310 --> 07:47.650
Weigh anchor!

07:47.650 --> 07:48.980
Aye aye, Sir!

07:49.090 --> 07:50.650
Helm, all to starboard!

07:50.650 --> 07:52.030
Aye aye, Sir!

07:52.030 --> 07:54.160
Off we go!

07:54.160 --> 07:56.160
Aye aye, Sir!

07:59.260 --> 08:02.560
Gekka-sama. Looks like everyone's gone.

08:10.320 --> 08:12.510
Just you watch, Do Gone.

08:12.510 --> 08:16.640
I will make you pay for standing against the Purple Skull Pirates!

08:16.640 --> 08:19.470
I will blast the airzooka, swing the flags, and-

08:25.170 --> 08:26.230
Hello.

08:27.100 --> 08:29.730
W-W-Wh-Why do we have civilians on board?

08:29.730 --> 08:33.100
I had my attention on Do Gone and didn't notice you all!

08:33.100 --> 08:37.410
You see, we didn't come out of curiosity.

08:37.410 --> 08:40.390
We're worried about Kyouka, as well,
so we hoped we could be of some help.

08:40.390 --> 08:43.040
Y-Yes. We want to help.

08:43.040 --> 08:44.670
We need to save Mom.

08:44.670 --> 08:47.300
Well, I don't care as long as you stay out of our way.

08:47.300 --> 08:50.440
But it's dangerous you know.
The ocean's a monster, and we're facing a pirate.

08:50.440 --> 08:52.980
I won't guarantee that you'll make it back to land alive.

08:52.980 --> 08:55.160
Hey, stop sitting around!

08:55.160 --> 08:57.780
If one person slacks, even what moves won't move!

08:57.780 --> 08:58.890
Aye aye, Sir!

08:58.890 --> 09:01.180
We are pirates!

09:03.060 --> 09:06.130
I shall be your translator when a monster shows up!

09:06.130 --> 09:07.760
Then I'll do the fighting.

09:07.760 --> 09:09.980
A ship like that, I can take down easily.

09:09.980 --> 09:12.990
Wait, wait. We need to do things peacefully.

09:12.990 --> 09:17.190
Ginichi-san. I've been telling you to be more manly, haven't I?

09:17.190 --> 09:18.900
Ah, Chika-chan, you're being scary.

09:18.900 --> 09:22.160
Hey now everyone. You've all forgotten about Kyouka, haven't you?

09:22.730 --> 09:27.530
Now, Do Gone's ship is fast, so how do we catch up?

09:27.530 --> 09:28.920
We'll take a shortcut.

09:29.730 --> 09:34.380
I have the treasure map memorized, so we'll take a shortcut there and get it before they can.

09:34.550 --> 09:37.380
Okay, we're far away enough from the land!

09:37.380 --> 09:39.510
Everyone, prepare for the shock!

09:39.920 --> 09:43.270
Electric Marching Wheel Navigation! Get, set, go!

09:43.270 --> 09:44.260
Electric!

09:44.260 --> 09:45.220
Marching?

09:45.220 --> 09:46.060
Wheel?

09:46.060 --> 09:46.890
Navigation?

09:46.890 --> 09:50.140
It accelerates electrically, and we'll outrun Do Gone!

09:50.140 --> 09:50.810
Electrically?

09:50.810 --> 09:51.900
Outrun them?

09:51.900 --> 09:54.030
Electric Marching Wheel Navigation, ready!

09:54.030 --> 09:56.030
Electric Marching Wheel Navigation, ready!

09:56.030 --> 09:58.690
All right, gang, get ready for this!

09:58.690 --> 10:00.370
We'll live through this and meet again!

10:00.370 --> 10:03.120
We'll meet again!

10:03.120 --> 10:04.500
What is this?

10:04.500 --> 10:06.270
It's very dangerous.

10:06.270 --> 10:08.160
Electric Marching Wheel Navigation!

10:08.160 --> 10:10.750
Dancing!

10:27.850 --> 10:28.810
Wh-What was that?

10:29.350 --> 10:31.440
Damn, Mujyakey. She took the lead.

10:33.270 --> 10:34.730
Hey, what's going on?

10:34.730 --> 10:38.130
They can't accelerate right after
Electric Marching Wheel Navigation.

10:38.130 --> 10:39.820
Scare them with some warning shots!

10:39.820 --> 10:40.570
Sir!

10:42.590 --> 10:44.580
Hey, don't ignore Kyouka-sama!

10:44.580 --> 10:46.950
Why do you pirates have such poor manners?!

10:48.450 --> 10:52.180
Gekka-sama, isn't that the direction your family went?

10:53.280 --> 10:54.130
Gekka-sama?

11:00.100 --> 11:01.160
It looks so itchy.

11:10.130 --> 11:11.690
Yuuka. Chika-san.

11:11.690 --> 11:13.060
Are you all fine?

11:13.060 --> 11:15.570
My eyes are simply spinning, Dad.

11:17.320 --> 11:19.440
Are you all fine?

11:19.440 --> 11:22.030
TF for totally fine.

11:22.660 --> 11:24.010
The world's spinning.

11:24.010 --> 11:26.450
C-Captain, are you all right?

11:26.450 --> 11:29.090
Deck chief, report the status.

11:29.090 --> 11:31.140
We did outrun them...

11:31.140 --> 11:32.080
It's dangerous.

11:32.080 --> 11:34.460
...but we couldn't gain as much distance as we wanted.

11:36.460 --> 11:37.800
They're right in front of us!

11:40.090 --> 11:40.960
Watch out!

11:43.910 --> 11:44.900
Kyouka.

11:44.450 --> 11:45.350
Mom.

11:45.790 --> 11:46.850
You were all right?

11:47.820 --> 11:49.720
Thank you, catperson.

11:51.100 --> 11:52.300
Give me hundred yen.

11:54.600 --> 11:55.610
Eh?

11:55.610 --> 11:56.610
Hundred yen?

11:56.610 --> 11:57.930
What's that?

11:58.880 --> 12:00.800
I said give me hundred yen for saving you!

12:02.290 --> 12:04.480
I see, so you can't pay hundred yen, eh?

12:04.480 --> 12:04.860
In that case!

12:06.320 --> 12:09.290
I, Kyouka-sama, am now the...

12:11.150 --> 12:12.920
...Captain!

12:15.330 --> 12:20.630
Everyone! Use every firearm you have
to repel Do Gone who kept ignoring me!

12:21.010 --> 12:23.930
Kyouka! We're glad to see you back safe,
and what are you doing now?!

12:23.930 --> 12:24.930
Fire!

12:26.220 --> 12:28.100
Sink their ship!

12:28.100 --> 12:29.970
They started shooting at us all of a sudden.

12:29.970 --> 12:31.730
Fire! Fire!

12:29.970 --> 12:31.730
Stop it!

12:32.290 --> 12:35.400
Observe the outcome of those who ignore me!

12:35.400 --> 12:37.230
You can't say you played shooting games until you've mastered the curtain fire game!

12:37.230 --> 12:38.900
It's a trip until you go home,

12:38.900 --> 12:41.570
and war continues until you annihilate your opponent!

12:41.570 --> 12:42.490
Stop it!

12:42.980 --> 12:44.960
Please stop this already!

12:44.960 --> 12:50.380
If a ship sinks in the middle of the sea,
everyone could really die!

12:50.380 --> 12:51.450
That's how it should be.

12:52.200 --> 12:53.320
That's good.

12:55.250 --> 12:57.590
That's how things go, Mujyakey!

12:57.590 --> 12:58.460
What?

13:11.140 --> 13:14.020
Let's cut it out, Kyouka.

13:14.020 --> 13:14.640
Okay?

13:14.640 --> 13:21.090
Yes. Since my hubby's staring at me with a scary look I've never seen before, but...

13:21.090 --> 13:25.700
Mujyakey! The ocean named for life isn't calm enough to let you through with just kindness.

13:27.270 --> 13:31.160
As your elder in life, I will teach you
the three important principles in life!

13:31.160 --> 13:32.590
Three principles?

13:32.590 --> 13:34.510
First! When done to you, return the favor!

13:34.510 --> 13:36.830
Second! Never show any mercy to your enemy!

13:36.830 --> 13:39.560
Third! Defeat your enemy when you have the chance!

13:39.560 --> 13:40.420
Kyouka!

13:40.420 --> 13:43.160
You group of regulars and some extras!

13:43.160 --> 13:45.390
Who do you think you are, having a party over there?!

13:45.390 --> 13:47.700
We were about to die and turn into a ghostship...

13:47.700 --> 13:52.670
...and become capable of saying only, "Give us a ladle..."

13:49.650 --> 13:53.330
No one's going to understand such an obscure ghost story.

13:52.670 --> 13:55.610
Shut up! You want it to be that big thing instead?

13:55.610 --> 13:59.740
That thing where no one knows
if it's an octopus, squid, or jelly fish?

14:00.620 --> 14:02.050
K-K-K-

14:02.520 --> 14:03.610
You mean Kraken?

14:03.610 --> 14:05.440
You can't say the name!

14:05.440 --> 14:08.200
What's a Kraken, Dad?

14:05.440 --> 14:08.200
You're not supposed to say its name.

14:08.200 --> 14:13.050
What? Kraken's just a squid monster. I saw it in a movie just the other day.

14:13.050 --> 14:16.330
That's right. Kraken's a really ugly monster.

14:19.280 --> 14:22.460
And you're supposed to be the daughter of Growald, who scared the entire world?

14:22.460 --> 14:24.000
What happened to the big speech you were making?

14:22.460 --> 14:24.000
Is there something wrong with Kraken?

14:24.950 --> 14:30.010
There's a legend that says anyone who calls its name will be attacked by it and get dragged into the water.

14:30.010 --> 14:32.300
Though, of course, it's only a legend.

14:36.270 --> 14:38.440
Look everyone! Something amazing popped up!

14:38.440 --> 14:39.310
Bring the camera!

14:39.310 --> 14:40.400
Can I attack?

14:40.400 --> 14:43.400
No, you idiot! We're going to capture it alive and show it off to people!

14:43.400 --> 14:45.680
Oh my god! It is a Kraken!

14:45.680 --> 14:47.350
Is it Kraken? Is it Kraken?

14:47.350 --> 14:48.780
Yes, it is Kraken!

14:48.780 --> 14:49.950
Kraken's so amazing!

14:49.950 --> 14:52.680
Kraken!

14:51.430 --> 14:52.680
Stop it!

14:52.680 --> 14:55.120
Or else Kraken will come to us!

14:59.030 --> 15:00.330
I can get rid of it, right?

15:01.300 --> 15:02.080
Everyone!

15:03.960 --> 15:05.750
We're done for!

15:15.410 --> 15:17.680
Everyone's late.

15:21.060 --> 15:22.270
Captain!

15:22.270 --> 15:23.460
Are you all right?

15:23.460 --> 15:24.470
What happened to the ship?

15:24.470 --> 15:27.520
We went through a lot, thanks to your puny ship sinking.

15:27.520 --> 15:30.880
Looks like we were saved by getting washed to this cave.

15:31.860 --> 15:33.000
Captain!

15:33.000 --> 15:37.220
I see. So the ship sunk, eh?

15:38.550 --> 15:39.470
This place is...

15:39.470 --> 15:40.210
Captain?

15:40.210 --> 15:43.240
What? Did you hit your head when the ship was sinking?

15:50.920 --> 15:55.300
There's no mistake! These are the ruins of the ancient civilization my father hid the treasure in!

15:55.300 --> 15:57.100
Captain! If that's true...

15:57.100 --> 15:58.180
Treasure!

15:58.180 --> 15:59.760
Father's assets.

16:00.590 --> 16:03.030
Are you going to go look for the treasure?

16:03.030 --> 16:04.180
We should probably wait for help to come.

16:04.180 --> 16:05.880
It's my father's assets.

16:05.880 --> 16:07.210
Yes! Treasures!

16:07.210 --> 16:11.010
It's the legendary pirate's treasure. What do you think it could be?

16:11.010 --> 16:12.980
Shining gold and silvers?

16:12.980 --> 16:14.000
Gold and silvers?!

16:14.000 --> 16:17.450
No, it's got to be something much more precious.

16:17.450 --> 16:18.620
Something much more precious?

16:18.620 --> 16:20.220
It has to be!

16:20.220 --> 16:25.270
If I use this treasure, everyone in the world, pirate or not, will become happy.

16:25.270 --> 16:27.410
Will live a happy life and will get to smile!

16:27.410 --> 16:31.820
Yes! The world exists for the sake of my happiness!
The treasure exists for my sake, too!

16:31.820 --> 16:34.460
Kyouka, can you refrain from making comments each time?

16:34.460 --> 16:37.100
Even if it involves lots or work or danger, I will move forward!

16:37.680 --> 16:39.600
Captain!

16:39.600 --> 16:41.770
Forward for the treasure!

16:41.770 --> 16:43.310
There's the treasure!

16:43.310 --> 16:44.240
That was fast.

16:44.240 --> 16:45.090
Yup, very fast.

16:45.090 --> 16:46.560
Hold it.

16:47.810 --> 16:48.900
That's as far as you get to go.

16:48.900 --> 16:49.690
Do Gone!

16:49.690 --> 16:52.280
Now, hand over the key.

16:52.280 --> 16:55.290
No! This is a treasure my father left behind!

16:55.290 --> 16:57.200
I'm going to use it for the sake of world peace!

16:57.200 --> 16:59.460
What kind of nonsense are you speaking?!

16:59.460 --> 17:01.380
If you're a pirate, pick up your weapon!

17:01.380 --> 17:01.870
You mean this?

17:01.870 --> 17:02.870
Not mackerel!

17:02.870 --> 17:03.450
This!

17:04.290 --> 17:04.960
I challenge you to a duel!

17:05.640 --> 17:07.820
Yes, kill each other.

17:07.820 --> 17:10.590
In the meantime, I will take the treasure away.

17:10.590 --> 17:12.450
You still haven't learned your lesson of the day?

17:12.450 --> 17:13.970
No, I was only joking.

17:13.970 --> 17:16.260
What's wrong? Scared?

17:16.260 --> 17:19.400
Crap. Captain's never shot a gun before.

17:19.400 --> 17:22.900
Guns can't protect everyone's happiness.

17:22.900 --> 17:24.520
This is wrong.

17:25.140 --> 17:30.740
If you can't protect your father's treasure or your men, then you have no right to talk about others' happiness!

17:30.740 --> 17:32.230
After all, you're just a baby talking.

17:32.230 --> 17:34.440
Do Gone! We don't care what happens to us!

17:34.440 --> 17:35.590
So keep your hands off of our Captain!

17:36.150 --> 17:36.940
Shut up!

17:36.940 --> 17:40.220
Those who have to power to trample the weak rule this world.

17:40.220 --> 17:41.160
That's what pirates are!

17:40.590 --> 17:41.160
You're wrong!

17:41.990 --> 17:46.190
Pirates are people who live and die on the seas to protect peace.

17:46.190 --> 17:48.490
A very noble blood runs through us.

17:48.490 --> 17:52.250
The pirate, Mujyakey Serpent will protect everyone!

18:06.260 --> 18:07.780
Lady....

18:08.850 --> 18:12.360
To be able to see you as such a great pirate...

18:12.360 --> 18:16.920
I, Do Gone, can now go to where Growald-sama is without any worry.

18:16.920 --> 18:19.990
Do Gone! Did you get shot on purpose?

18:20.840 --> 18:21.950
Why?

18:23.600 --> 18:24.580
Why?!

18:24.580 --> 18:28.240
No! No! Don't die!

18:37.130 --> 18:38.940
Do Gone!

18:38.940 --> 18:42.560
Now, Lady. Please take your father's assets.

18:42.560 --> 18:46.110
We are pirates.

18:46.110 --> 18:49.580
Pirates, pirates, pirates we tell you.

18:49.580 --> 18:52.900
Ah, ah, let's go.

19:01.070 --> 19:02.140
Father!

19:02.140 --> 19:03.030
Growald-sama!

19:03.030 --> 19:06.830
You've come far, my cute Mujyakey.

19:06.830 --> 19:08.360
Father!

19:08.360 --> 19:12.210
I am the great pirate, Growald. The man who got everything.

19:12.210 --> 19:14.960
But there was one thing that I worried about in my death bed.

19:14.960 --> 19:17.580
And that's Mujyakey, your future.

19:17.580 --> 19:18.620
My future?

19:18.620 --> 19:21.650
You're too kind to be a pirate. Too weak!

19:21.650 --> 19:23.830
Pirates are supposed to be more heartless.

19:23.830 --> 19:28.310
So right before I died, I asked Do Gone,
the vice-captain, to give you a challenge.

19:29.050 --> 19:32.470
If you're so weak that you can't outrun Do Gone and get the treasure,

19:32.470 --> 19:37.650
then it's better for you to step on land and live as a normal child.

19:37.650 --> 19:41.220
However you made it to the treasure!

19:41.220 --> 19:44.840
Mujyakey, you indeed are the daughter of Growald.

19:44.840 --> 19:46.840
I'm sure the road taken wasn't easy.

19:46.840 --> 19:48.650
The strength to overcome the challenge.

19:48.650 --> 19:50.130
The courage to face the adversary.

19:50.130 --> 19:51.550
The will to see through your objective.

19:51.550 --> 19:54.980
You should find those as your treasure in you.

19:54.980 --> 19:58.000
That is the asset I leave behind for you!

19:58.000 --> 20:03.160
Never forget that and strive to be a great pirate!

20:03.160 --> 20:06.370
Growald-sama!

20:04.950 --> 20:07.890
Ah, this is the punch line?

20:09.380 --> 20:13.180
In other words, there is no gold and silver?

20:13.740 --> 20:14.740
What?

20:14.740 --> 20:17.970
By the way, I hid all the gold and silver in a secret place.

20:17.970 --> 20:22.510
If you'd get a hold of my assets that easily,
you'd become a worthless adult who won't work.

20:22.510 --> 20:27.280
I didn't make a map for it, so do
your best at searching for it, pirate Mujyakey!

20:27.660 --> 20:29.360
Wow, that's mean!

20:29.360 --> 20:30.590
Wait!

20:30.590 --> 20:31.790
How could you!

20:30.890 --> 20:32.430
Lady!

20:32.560 --> 20:34.470
Do Gone's ecstatic!

20:34.470 --> 20:36.310
You've become amazing!

20:38.730 --> 20:39.670
Lady?

20:40.170 --> 20:41.120
Hundred yen.

20:41.120 --> 20:41.710
Eh?

20:41.960 --> 20:43.830
I said pay me hundred yen.

20:43.830 --> 20:44.630
For all the troubles you've caused.

20:45.360 --> 20:47.590
Huh? Lady?

20:47.590 --> 20:49.180
Didn't you hear me?

20:49.180 --> 20:54.450
Or if you can't pay the hundred yen,
do you want to give your ship to me?

20:54.450 --> 20:55.560
Th-That's...

20:55.560 --> 20:59.850
Strength and courage won't fill our stomach!

21:01.070 --> 21:02.750
This is the result of living peacefully.

21:02.750 --> 21:04.660
I won't believe in anything anymore!

21:04.660 --> 21:06.780
Gold and silver are everything to this world!

21:06.780 --> 21:10.070
You're a true pirate!

21:10.070 --> 21:13.160
You indeed are the daughter of the cold-hearted Growald!

21:13.160 --> 21:15.920
Treasure... Treasure... Treasure...

21:13.650 --> 21:15.920
Things are clearly looking bad.

21:15.920 --> 21:18.100
Mujyakey-chan, you're simply scary.

21:18.100 --> 21:20.320
Sensor responding red. Sensor responding red.

21:20.340 --> 21:23.550
Woah, hold it. You think I would just let you guys go?

21:23.550 --> 21:25.170
You with the cat ears!

21:25.170 --> 21:27.730
When done to you, return the favor, right?

21:27.730 --> 21:30.470
Oh, did I say something like that?

21:30.470 --> 21:33.140
Show no mercy to your enemy, was it?

21:33.140 --> 21:36.270
H-Hey, whoever taught you that?

21:36.270 --> 21:38.180
And what was the third principle?

21:39.390 --> 21:40.650
It's...

21:41.060 --> 21:43.860
I forgot!

21:52.690 --> 21:54.580
Gekka-sama. Welcome back.

21:55.150 --> 21:56.580
Hey, that flag is...

21:56.580 --> 21:58.780
That's the pirate's flag.

22:00.960 --> 22:03.250
It's itchy!

22:04.810 --> 22:09.480
It's itchy! It's itchy! It's itchy!

23:40.850 --> 23:43.040
Hyouka, if it's painful, you can cry.

23:43.040 --> 23:45.440
Your sister will simply listen to you.

23:45.440 --> 23:48.120
Yuuka, have you ever fallen in love? Have you ever been rejected? Do you have a person you're dating?

23:48.120 --> 23:50.200
Have you ever been on a date? Was it your classmate? Or maybe someone older than you?

23:50.200 --> 23:51.820
It can't be someone younger than you, right?

23:50.780 --> 23:53.910
N-Next time: Hyouka's First Love.
